 "notes": "JEDI/COSY storage-ring scan, spin-precession resonance 120.0-121.4 kHz (ma = 0.4963-0.5023 neV). Headline 90% CL limit: oscillating deuteron EDM |d_d^AC| < 6.4e-23 e cm (Eq. 37, average over scan), equivalent to |g_adgamma| < 1.7e-7 GeV^-2 (Eq. 38). Curve extracted from vector paths of Fig. 17 (figures/sensitivity_plot_atten.pdf in e-print): both ramp-rate curves (green dp=0.112 MeV/c for 120.0-120.25 kHz, blue dp=0.138 MeV/c for 120.25-121.46 kHz) combined, bin-averaged to 90 points, and converted per point via Eq. 38: g = (d/e hbar c) sqrt(4 pi alpha)/a0 with a0 = sqrt(2 rho (hbar c)^3)/ma, rho_LDM = 0.55 GeV/cm^3 (conversion verified: 6.4e-23 e cm -> 1.69e-7 GeV^-2, matching the paper). Reported coupling is the deuteron EDM operator coupling g_adgamma, the deuteron analog of the canonical nucleon g_d (d = g a); the paper plots it in the |g_aNgamma| [GeV^-2] plane (Fig. 19). The axion-wind (Cd/fa < 1.5e-5 GeV^-1) and gluon-coupling (Cd_G/fa < 0.46e-4 GeV^-1) bounds from the same data are secondary results not reported here.",
